tilda swinton is an actor like no other  with wide-ranging roles in films like  doctor strange and suspiria  it may have been a while since winton's  last big movie but that doesn't mean she  hasn't been busy  here's why you may not have seen very  much of swinton lately  when swinton first began her acting  career she moved to london to work with  the royal shakespeare company  however she moved back to her childhood  home of scotland once she had grown  tired of the city life  a small town homebody at heart she has  made a comfortable life for herself and  her family in the scottish highlands  as she said in an interview for esquire  i mean i've even lost the way of living  in a city  if i had to live in a city again it  would take me a long time  you have to train up to live in a city  today swinton says that she rarely  visits london anymore and feels that she  is out of touch with the industry there  although she does occasionally think  about moving back to a city  she has no plans to do so in the near  future  swinton has fans all around the world  but she couldn't tell you what they're  saying about her online  thanks to her decision to stay off  social media entirely  the actor considers herself a quote  complete luddite  telling vogue i have no presence on  social media  absolutely none i just have other things  to do  i know what's going on it's like there's  a forest on fire somewhere down the end  of the garden  but i'm concentrating on the roses while  swinton's fans would probably  love to see her on twitter or instagram  it's unlikely she'll be creating an  account anytime soon  application tonight i'm sorry despite  her bulky resume  swinton insists that she is not an  ambitious person saying  i've never had any ambition as an artist  that may sound crazy and transgressive  but it's a fact in fact swinton has  admitted that she does not even think of  herself as a traditional actress  even though she's been acting for over  30 years while she will certainly accept  the opportunity to appear in a  blockbuster franchise when the chance  comes around  she isn't specifically seeking out these  roles and swinton doesn't go to  auditions anymore either  she's accomplished enough that directors  come to her overall she will always put  passion over potential profits  for swinton the director she's working  with is often more important than the  film itself  she has worked at least three times each  with directors wes anderson  jim jarmisch and luca guadagnino in the  early years of her career she worked  closely with director derek jarman  on several more experimental films which  taught her that supportive relationships  with directors who shared her vision  were the key to artistic fulfillment in  an interview swinton told the  independent  we are used to actors moving from  project to project in a slightly  detached  way or that they are looking over their  shoulder for a more interesting project  or more money  but that is not how i approach it i need  to work with people that i can trust  i always choose the people first swinton  is far more likely to wait for an  intriguing  role with the right director even if it  means passing up roles that other actors  might have jumped at  swinton knows that a great film can take  time which is why she's willing to spend  several years patiently working to give  a single project the attention  it deserves swinton states that this  kind of focused  long-term attention makes her process  unique allowing her to personally  develop her roles alongside her  directors and writers  she revealed to variety most people  don't develop work the way i  customarily do they'll wait for someone  to place them into their universe with  proper craftspeople  whereas i spend most of my time sitting  around my kitchen table with friends  chewing on ideas and building things  that take years  swinton spent five years working on the  film orlando with director sally potter  and she dedicated quote seven or eight  years to  only lovers left alive she even spent as  many as 11 years committed to her role  in  i am love learning both russian and  italian to make her character seem as  realistic as possible  swinton's name rarely makes it into the  tabloids and even when it does  she isn't very interested in joining in  the conversation rarely feeling the need  to clarify details about her  personal and romantic life with the  press in fact it often takes her a while  to hear through the grapevine if there  is a rumor spreading about her in the  first place  she joked i'm playful at heart and myth  making is always fun  for instance when swinton began dating  artist sandro copp  the press speculated that she had first  gotten together with cop during her  relationship with her previous partner  of 14 years  playwright john byrne the gossip spread  for years before swinton realized what  was being said and had to come forward  to state that it was nothing but a rumor  i mean this is really inappropriate  if swinton hasn't been filming  blockbusters what has she been working  on  while fans of swinton might have caught  her latest big name projects  some of her recent work has flown under  the radar in 2020 she lent her voice to  the late composer johann johansson for  his experimental film  last and first men the movie explores a  futuristic society in which evolved  humans face potential extinction  and surreal monuments beam out messages  into the universe  swinton also worked on several short  films in 2020  she narrated story and the writer which  explored a man's efforts to write the  perfect screenplay  in addition she appeared in pedro  almodovars the human voice  in which she played a woman who notes  the passing of time while she waits for  her ex-lover to come and pick up his  suitcases  while the short was not widely viewed it  did receive some glowing reviews  as critic ryan rojas wrote in a review  for cinemasy  tilda swinton commands every second of  the small screen in pedro almodovar's  beautifully staged and winkingly meta  new short film in august 2020  the personal history of david  copperfield was released  armando yanuchi's comedic drama adapted  charles dickens classic story for the  modern age  starring dev patel as the title  character swinton portrayed betsy  trotwood  david copperfield's eccentric great aunt  who takes him in  and ends up financing his dream of  becoming an author  oh my lawn unbox your ears  off you go this is a donkey free zone  move it  although critics held a generally  positive opinion of the film  that didn't prevent it from being a flop  at the box office  the timing of its release certainly  didn't help as the film arrived in  theaters in the midst of the covid19  pandemic  once a majority of movie theaters had  temporarily closed down for safety  reasons  the pandemic disrupted the production  schedule for countless movies and tv  shows  many directors had to postpone shooting  for months on end  leaving lots of release dates in limbo  while some studios have chosen to  release their new films through  streaming services  others have decided simply to delay  their releases  meaning audiences will have to wait a  little while longer to see them  that was the case for swinton's highly  anticipated movie the french dispatch  the wes anderson flick was originally  slated for a july 2020 release  likely at the cannes film festival  however the festival was cancelled  because of the coven 19 pandemic  and the tentative release date was  pushed to october 2020  which was again postponed until 2021  swinton also has experience behind the  camera she's currently working on a  documentary about progressive education  systems around the world  swinton has been interested in creating  schools that encourage students to reach  their full potential for years  having co-founded the drumduin upper  school in scotland where her own  children attended  the school does not require students to  take tests or even sit at desks most of  the time  so it's likely that her documentary will  focus on unorthodox approaches to  education  this won't be swinton's first time  directing in 2008 she was one of several  directors for the documentary  the new ten commandments which explores  human rights in scotland  and in 2016 she collaborated with  several other directors for the film  the seasons in quincy four portraits of  john berger  a tribute to the respected novelist  while it might seem like swinton has  been laying low  she has been as busy as ever having been  working on several upcoming projects for  some time  first up is her film the souvenir part  two  a sequel to her 2019 film the souvenir  in which she stars alongside her  daughter  honor swinton byrne her movie the  eternal daughter is also anticipated to  release in 2021  multiple upcoming swinton films have yet  to gain official release dates  but fans can expect to see her in films  such as the fantasy epic  3000 years of longing and the drama  memoria  she's also going to be voicing the fairy  with turquoise hair  and guillermo del toro's dark adaptation  of the classic story  pinocchio check out one of our newest  videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

